  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Ambiente</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Governance in the Maya Biosphere Reserve</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Guatemala):  With FY 2024 funding, the U.S. Department of the Interior&apos;s International Technical Assistance Program (DOI-ITAP) and USAID aim to strengthen governance in the Selva Maya. This initiative will build capacity and resilience against illegal activities by partnering with the National Council for Protected Areas (CONAP), universities, local communities, and NGOs. USAID&apos;s efforts will enhance governance, improve protected area management, and engage local stakeholders to safeguard the region&apos;s natural resources...The program focuses on seven objectives: strengthening local governance and civil society; enhancing protected area management; supporting judicial cases; protecting biodiversity; promoting social safeguards; expanding outreach and communication; and facilitating sustainable income generation...By fostering cross-border collaboration among Guatemala, Belize, and Mexico, the program will improve coordination and empower communities through sustainable livelihoods, such as community-based tourism. These efforts reduce the appeal of illicit activities and promote lawful economic alternatives...With a $2.5 million allocation, this activity supports U.S. strategic goals, including the Root Causes Strategy and the Joint Strategic Plan, while advancing environmental governance and sustainable development. USAID&apos;s investment in the Selva Maya enhances regional stability, combats illegal activity, and protects critical ecosystems, aligning with both U.S. security interests...$2.5M of funding within this IM contributes to meeting the required $2.5M of the Environment - Guatemala and Belize and Mexico Directive..</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Garantizar que el medio ambiente y los recursos naturales de los que dependen las vidas y los medios de subsistencia humanos se gestionen de manera que sostengan la productividad y el crecimiento, as&#xed; como una poblaci&#xf3;n sana.</narrative>
  </description>
